### What happened?

Since the last protocol 15.11, pressing a hotkey for a healing spell (or any instant spell) while paralyzed intermittently does nothing - no error message, no visual feedback, the spell simply doesn't fire, which is not the expected behavior. The behavior is random because it depends on timing. It does not affect potions/items used via hotkey (those correctly show "You are exhausted").

This was confirmed working correctly in the previous 15.00 and behaving badly in this last 15.11.

**Cause**
Two things combined to create the bug:

1. New function updateParalyzeWalkExhaust() was added in 15.11 (src/creatures/players/player.cpp):

  void Player::updateParalyzeWalkExhaust() {
      if (!hasCondition(CONDITION_PARALYZE)) { return; }
      const int32_t walkDelay = getWalkDelay();
      if (walkDelay > 0) {
          setWalkExhaust(walkDelay);
      }
  }   
This function is now called on onAddCondition(CONDITION_PARALYZE), onAddCombatCondition(CONDITION_PARALYZE), and on every onCreatureMove while paralyzed. It sets lastWalking = OTSYS_TIME() + walkDelay  (typically ~400ms).

2. playerSaySpell in game.cpp has a silent early-return on walkExhausted():

  bool Game::playerSaySpell(...) {
      if (player->walkExhausted()) {
          return true;  
      }
      ...
  }
  walkExhausted() returns true when hasCondition(CONDITION_PARALYZE) && lastWalking > OTSYS_TIME().

previously, setWalkExhaust() was defined but never called anywhere, so lastWalking was always 0 and walkExhausted() was effectively dead code - always false.

In the last 15.11, setWalkExhaust() is now actively called via updateParalyzeWalkExhaust(), making walkExhausted() return true for ~400ms whenever a paralyze condition is applied or the player moves while paralyzed.
During that window, any spell cast silently fails.

**Why this is wrong behavior**
In Tibia, paralyze slows movement speed but does not block spell casting. Players can and should be able to cast spells (including healing) while paralyzed. The walkExhausted() check in playerSaySpell was harmless dead code before 15.11 but became an unintended gameplay regression.

**Fix**

Remove the walkExhausted() check from Game::playerSaySpell in src/game/game.cpp:
Effectively going back to the 15.00 behavior.

bool Game::playerSaySpell(const std::shared_ptr<Player> &player, SpeakClasses type, const std::string &text) {
     if (player->walkExhausted()) {
             return true;
     }
     std::string words = text;

**Steps to reproduce**
1. Fight any monster that can apply paralyze, like run on roshamuul. You will see that you can heal and probably be sent to the temple.
2. Spam a healing spell hotkey while paralyzed
3. Observe that the spell intermittently (and kind of randomly) does nothing with no feedback.


### What OS are you seeing the problem on?

Linux

